INSTALL
-------

To compile xzgv, you’ll need the following packages:

Gtk+ 2 development files (libgtk2.0-dev on Debian/Ubuntu; gtk2.0-dev on
Fedora/SuSE)
pkg-config
make

Check `config.mk' to see if there's anything there you want to change
(most likely, the installation PREFIX).

After that, run `make' then `make install'. This compiles xzgv, then
installs it and its documentation (both info files and man page).


xzgv is regularly built for GNU/Linux; please report problems on other
platforms.


Good luck!
